; Fleet Splint config — copied byte-identical to .splint.edn in each
; adopted repo (see cljfmt.edn header for the sync law). v1 runs ALL
; default Splint rules: the Phase 1 census measures the default gate.
; A rule is disabled only fleet-wide, here, with the reason recorded —
; never per repo to make a repo pass. Where a Splint rule duplicates a
; clj-kondo idiom linter, the dedup choice is recorded here too.
; ── Repo-local exceptions (eve, Phase 2; proposed to the fleet in
; RETRO.md). Splint 1.25 has no per-path config: a rule is excepted
; per file through the rule's :excludes matchers, so every excepted
; file is named below and every other file keeps every rule.
;
; style/prefer-clj-math (7 files): the flagged calls name the HOST
; Math face (Math/floor, Math/log, Math/addExact, ...) in portable
; .cljc code and in Eve's own math facade — that spelling is the
; portability layer: every Eve host provides Math, while
; clojure.math exists only on JVM-Clojure-shaped seats. In
; host_completion the Math/*Exact calls ARE the checked-arithmetic
; primitives the seat wraps; in the flat-io conformance test the
; host Math face is the probe subject.
; lint/prefer-method-values (67 files, 847 findings): Splint's
; suggestion is not actionable as printed in this repo — every
; one of the 847 suggestions emits a literal CLASS placeholder
; ((CLASS/.method ...) etc.), because the receiver's class is
; not known to it. The receivers are host-seat values: the same
; portable .cljc form runs on JVM classes on :clj seats, JS
; objects on :cljs seats, Dart objects on :cljd seats, so no
; single Class/method spelling exists for the source to carry;
; the method-call / #(.m %) spelling IS the portability layer.
; Excepted per file below; every other file keeps the rule.
